Theorem (Congruence Rule for Triangles):
Given three triangles \(A, B, C\) and \(A1, B1, C1\) with corresponding sides and angles, if the sum of the sides of triangle \(A\) is congruent to the sum of the sides of triangle \(A1\), and the sum of the angles at \(B\) in both triangles is congruent, then the sum of the sides of triangle \(A\) is congruent to the sum of the sides of triangle \(A1\).

